.TH STRALLOC_CASE_STARTS 3 "2023-10-15" "c-utils" "String Allocation Functions"
.SH NAME
 stralloc_case_starts \- Check if a string starts with lowercase letters
.SH LIBRARY
 libstralloc
.SH SYNOPSIS
 .B #include <stralloc/stralloc.h>

 .B int
 stralloc_case_starts(const char *s);
.SH DESCRIPTION
 Returns non-zero if the string s starts with lowercase letters, zero otherwise.
 This function is used for case-sensitive string validation in the c-utils library.
.SH RETURN VALUES
 Non-zero if the string starts with lowercase letters, zero otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
 stralloc_case_ends(3), stralloc_isalpha(3)
